- [Skill](https://docs.cdp.coinbase.com/coinbase-for-agents/skill.md): Connect to Coinbase to trade crypto, US derivatives (futures), and US equities, pay for premium data via x402, manage portfolios, check prices, and convert currencies. Use when the user wants to place or preview orders, manage portfolios, transfer funds between portfolios, pay for market data or res…
- [Aerodrome Plugin](https://docs.cdp.coinbase.com/coinbase-for-agents/wallet-mcp/plugins/aerodrome.md): Swap, provide liquidity, stake, and claim rewards on Aerodrome.
- [Avantis Plugin](https://docs.cdp.coinbase.com/coinbase-for-agents/wallet-mcp/plugins/avantis.md): Open and manage leveraged perpetual-futures positions on Avantis.
- [Balancer Plugin](https://docs.cdp.coinbase.com/coinbase-for-agents/wallet-mcp/plugins/balancer.md): Swaps and liquidity on Balancer through a shell: read pools/quotes from the Balancer API, build calldata with the Balancer SDK, submit via send_calls. CLI-only — requires terminal access; unsupported on chat-only surfaces.
- [Bankr Plugin](https://docs.cdp.coinbase.com/coinbase-for-agents/wallet-mcp/plugins/bankr.md): Discover and buy newly launched tokens on Bankr.
- [Bitrefill Plugin](https://docs.cdp.coinbase.com/coinbase-for-agents/wallet-mcp/plugins/bitrefill.md): Shop 1,500+ brands in 180+ countries — Amazon, Steam, Netflix, mobile top-ups, and travel eSIMs — paid with USDC on Base. Your agent searches, checks out, and delivers gift-card codes and eSIM details in chat. No Bitrefill account required.
- [Brickken Plugin](https://docs.cdp.coinbase.com/coinbase-for-agents/wallet-mcp/plugins/brickken.md): ERC-8004 identity, reputation, and agent-token operations through Brickken with Wallet MCP x402 approval.
- [Clawnch Plugin](https://docs.cdp.coinbase.com/coinbase-for-agents/wallet-mcp/plugins/clawnch.md): Token-launch discovery (recent + top-by-volume) and non-custodial token launches on Clawnch via HTTP API → swap / send_calls on Base.
- [Flaunch Plugin](https://docs.cdp.coinbase.com/coinbase-for-agents/wallet-mcp/plugins/flaunch.md): Prepare Flaunch launches through mcp.flaunch.gg and submit them with Wallet MCP send_calls; discover and swap deployed tokens through Wallet MCP.
- [GMGN Plugin](https://docs.cdp.coinbase.com/coinbase-for-agents/wallet-mcp/plugins/gmgn.md): Token swap quotes and on-chain market intelligence for Base via GMGN API. Requires shell to generate auth parameters; returns unsigned calldata for send_calls execution.
- [Hydrex Plugin](https://docs.cdp.coinbase.com/coinbase-for-agents/wallet-mcp/plugins/hydrex.md): Swapping and concentrated-liquidity on Hydrex via local prepare server → send_calls on Base.
- [KyberSwap Plugin](https://docs.cdp.coinbase.com/coinbase-for-agents/wallet-mcp/plugins/kyberswap.md): DEX aggregation on KyberSwap via HTTP API → send_calls across 7 chains, best-rate routing through 50+ liquidity sources.
- [Moonwell Plugin](https://docs.cdp.coinbase.com/coinbase-for-agents/wallet-mcp/plugins/moonwell.md): Lend, borrow, and manage positions on Moonwell.
- [Morpho Plugin](https://docs.cdp.coinbase.com/coinbase-for-agents/wallet-mcp/plugins/morpho.md): Lend, borrow, and manage vault or market positions on Morpho.
- [o1.exchange Plugin](https://docs.cdp.coinbase.com/coinbase-for-agents/wallet-mcp/plugins/o1-exchange.md): Token trading on o1.exchange via HTTP API → send_calls on Base, and BSC.
- [OpenSea Plugin](https://docs.cdp.coinbase.com/coinbase-for-agents/wallet-mcp/plugins/opensea.md): NFT marketplace trading, token swaps, and drops/minting via OpenSea REST API + CLI → send_calls on Ethereum, Base, Polygon, Arbitrum, Optimism, and Avalanche.
- [Printr Plugin](https://docs.cdp.coinbase.com/coinbase-for-agents/wallet-mcp/plugins/printr.md): Launch cross-chain tokens on Printr via its public HTTP API → submit the unsigned creation calldata through Wallet MCP send_calls.
- [Uniswap Plugin](https://docs.cdp.coinbase.com/coinbase-for-agents/wallet-mcp/plugins/uniswap.md): Swap tokens and manage liquidity positions on Uniswap.
- [Venice AI Plugin](https://docs.cdp.coinbase.com/coinbase-for-agents/wallet-mcp/plugins/venice.md): Private AI inference through the Venice API, with optional Base x402 wallet funding via Wallet MCP.
- [Virtuals Plugin](https://docs.cdp.coinbase.com/coinbase-for-agents/wallet-mcp/plugins/virtuals.md): Create and manage Virtuals AI agents, cards, and email.
- [YO Protocol Plugin](https://docs.cdp.coinbase.com/coinbase-for-agents/wallet-mcp/plugins/yo.md): View YO vaults, check positions, deposit, and request redeem on YO's ERC-4626 yield vaults — fully on-chain reads via chain_rpc_request and unsigned calldata to send_calls on Base, Ethereum, and Arbitrum.
- [Approval Mode](https://docs.cdp.coinbase.com/coinbase-for-agents/wallet-mcp/references/approval-mode.md): Skill reference for how Wallet MCP returns approval URLs and request IDs for every write call.
- [Batched Contract Calls](https://docs.cdp.coinbase.com/coinbase-for-agents/wallet-mcp/references/batch-calls.md): Skill reference for Wallet MCP's EIP-5792 batched contract calls.
- [Custom Plugins and the web_request Allowlist](https://docs.cdp.coinbase.com/coinbase-for-agents/wallet-mcp/references/custom-plugins.md): Skill reference for how Wallet MCP routes plugin HTTP calls and which surfaces are allowlisted.
- [Installing Wallet MCP](https://docs.cdp.coinbase.com/coinbase-for-agents/wallet-mcp/references/install.md): Skill reference for installing the Wallet MCP server in Claude, ChatGPT, Cursor, Codex, and other surfaces.
- [Wallet MCP Plugin Specification](https://docs.cdp.coinbase.com/coinbase-for-agents/wallet-mcp/references/plugin-spec.md): Authoring spec for native Wallet MCP plugins — frontmatter schema, required body sections, integration types, and step-by-step instructions for writing or adapting a plugin to the spec.
- [Tone](https://docs.cdp.coinbase.com/coinbase-for-agents/wallet-mcp/references/tone.md): Skill reference for the language and tone rules an agent should follow when using Wallet MCP.
- [Wallet MCP Skill](https://docs.cdp.coinbase.com/coinbase-for-agents/wallet-mcp/skill.md): Wallet MCP — gives your AI assistant access to a Coinbase Wallet via the Wallet MCP server (wallet-mcp.coinbase.com). Wallet, portfolio, sending, swapping, signing, x402 payments, batched contract calls, and transaction history across supported chains.
